<title>POLAND: POLISH 52-WEEK T-BILL MINIMUM PRICE DOWN.</title>
<headline>POLISH 52-WEEK T-BILL MINIMUM PRICE DOWN.</headline>
<dateline>WARSAW 1997-06-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>The minimum prices of Poland's</p>
<p>52-week T-bill eased at Wednesday's primary auction on total</p>
<p>demand of 522 million zlotys against a 600 million zloty offer,</p>
<p>the finance ministry said.</p>
<p>The minstry sold 382 million zlotys worth of bills today.</p>
<p>The finance minstry also said it would stage a 1.3 million</p>
<p>zloty primary T-bill tender on Monday, June 23.</p>
<p> T-bill	     13-week  26-week  52-week</p>
<p>  new min price    ---	---	82.08</p>
<p> (pvs auction)     ---	---     (82.11)</p>
<p>  new max price    ---	---	82.20</p>
<p> (pvs auction)     ---	---     (86.03)</p>
<p>  offer		---	---	600.0</p>
<p>  bids recorded    ---	---	522.3</p>
<p>  bids accepted    ---	---	381.7</p>
<p> next auction     200.0    200.0     900.0</p>
<p>NOTE- Offer and bids in million zlotys. The payment date for</p>
<p>the next auction is June 25. -- Warsaw Newsroom +48 22 653 9700</p>
</text>
